WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.489 --> 00:00:04.500
Where I come from

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.839
respect for authority almost silenced us.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.530
We are taught from a young age

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.030
never to speak back to elders

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.450
and especially those in positions of influence and authority.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:14.610
But this is changing

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.410
and that’s all thanks to social media.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.340
There is a young generation of Kenyans

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.050
who are using this space as a safe place for dissent.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.109
Young people like me are watching in real
time

00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:25.120
how the world around them

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.820
is surprisingly similar

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.250
and using online spaces

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.940
to create global conversations.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.710
I remember hearing about officials in our
sports ministry

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.600
allegedly misappropriating funds

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.670
meant for our Olympic athletes.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.210
Young Kenyans armed with nothing but hashtags

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.140
took to twitter and facebook and made their voice heard.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.760
It was a perfect example of brotherhood,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.030
nationalism and a call for accountability

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.290
140 characters at a time.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:52.530
It’s really important for me

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.239
to listen to these emerging voices

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:55.960
of this young continent

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.500
and tell their stories.

